{
  "exp_id": "EXP-4",
  "title": "Schema errors",
  "hypothesis": "A renamed required column is detected and a mapping proposed but not applied without approval; prices are fixed by try_cast and quarantine; the missing optional table disables its features.",
  "independent_variable": "fault type",
  "dependent_measures": [
    "detected",
    "correct_action",
    "mapping_proposed",
    "approval_requests",
    "auto_applied_without_a_person",
    "time_to_recovery_s",
    "cleaning_succeeded",
    "quarantined_rows",
    "row_accounting_balanced",
    "customer_service_group",
    "wall_clock_s"
  ],
  "started_at": "2026-10-09T18:48:42.971332+00:00",
  "duration_s": 1863.47,
  "status": "completed",
  "hypothesis_held": true,
  "conclusion": "Detected at: renamed_required_column -> ingest, price_as_text_with_symbols -> clean, dropped_optional_table -> features. 3 of 3 faults detected and 3 handled correctly; the clean baseline passed: True. The renamed column was refused at ingest with the mapping cust_id -> customer_id proposed and a schema_change approval requested; while it was pending nothing was registered and applying it was refused, and once approved the mapped copy registered and cleaned with balanced rows 229.7 s after the decision. Prices written as text were fixed: the column was converted with try_cast and 0 value(s) that did not convert were quarantined, with the row accounting balanced. Without the support tickets table the feature job marked the customer service group unavailable and produced none of its 6 features, which the baseline produced. 0 mappings were applied without a person. 0 conditions lost rows silently (cleaning reported success while the row accounting did not balance). Detection is measured against the baseline on purpose: a detector that flagged everything would otherwise score perfectly.",
  "limitations": [
    "`register_version` returns early on an identical checksum, before it validates anything. That is correct idempotence, but it means a file whose bytes were registered before a contract existed for its dataset is never re-validated. This experiment sidesteps it by registering each condition under a fresh dataset name; a deployment would need a re-validation pass when a contract is introduced or changed. Not a defect, but not covered either.",
    "The proposed mapping was approved by the harness acting as a Data Engineer, so the time to recovery covers the platform's work after the decision and not the time a person would take to make it."
  ],
